  "method": "The first byte and all subsequent chunks used real read readiness. Exactly 256 KiB promoted only the tested direction. On an open connection, a 17-byte trailer produced no read event before the timer; after demotion it was readable and the connection remained open. With FIN, the high watermark remained active, including if a timer event was already pending. The first EV_EOF carried 17 unread bytes, the next carried zero, and the peer received the bytes before its EOF. The reverse marker succeeded in each case. The open-row wait times measure time spent waiting in the fixture for the configured 2 ms timer; dispatch time depends on scheduling.",
